ANSWER OF CONSTELLATION ENERGY GENERATION, LLC 
Constellation1 submits this answer to support PJM’s motion extending the compliance 
deadline for implementing changes to Contract Demand Services2 among other changes with one 
clarification:3 that PJM remains obligated to file on August 17, 2026, a complete set of provisions 

1 Constellation Energy Generation, LLC (“Constellation”) files this answer pursuant to Rule 213 of the Commission’s 
Rules of Practice and Procedure. See 18 C.F.R. § 385.213. 
2 Contract Demand Services refers collectively to Firm Contract Demand Transmission Service (“Firm Contract 
Demand Service”) and Non-Firm Contract Demand Transmission Service (“Non-Firm Contract Demand Service”). 
3 See Motion for Extension of Time for Specified Compliance Requirements and Request for Expedited Treatment of 
PJM Interconnection, L.L.C., at 7 (July 28, 2026) (PJM requests an extension to comply with Commission directives 
other than “certain defined terms in Tariff, Part I; certain terms for NITS pursuant to Tariff, Part III; additional 
details regarding the Necessary Study process that will be specified in the manuals; and the provision of 
interim NITS”) (“Motion for Extension of Time”).
